<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23554" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαύχνα</span></b> , Thess., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάφνη</span>
			, found only in compds. (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχιδαυχναφορέω</span>) :—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαυχνοφόρος</span></b> , 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαφνηφόρος</span>
			, cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				17
			</span></i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαυχναφόριος</span></b> ,
				ὁ, prob. epith. of Apollo in Cyprus,
				<i>Ber.Sächs.Ges.</i><i><span class="en">
				1908.3
			</span></i>; cf. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαυχναῖος</span></b> ,
			patron. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαύχνας,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(2).1228.26
			</span></i>. (Perh. akin not to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάφνη,</span>
			but to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαῦκος.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
